From: ccbench-remote
Subject: [PATCH] report.py: move the PDF across filesystems, not rename(2)

src/analysis/report.py renders the report into utils.tmp_dir (/pantheon/tmp,
inside the image) and then moves it to the data dir with os.rename(). We
bind-mount the data dir from the host, so the two paths are on different
filesystems and rename(2) fails with EXDEV:

    OSError: [Errno 18] Invalid cross-device link
      File "/pantheon/src/analysis/report.py", line 332, in run
        os.rename(pdf_src_path, pdf_dst_path)

OBSERVED, 2026-11-04 matrix: all four schemes. The PDF itself was fine --
pdflatex reported "Output written on pantheon_report_<uid>.pdf (5 pages,
187682 bytes)" -- but the failed move propagated up through analyze.py:

    subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['python',
      '/pantheon/src/analysis/report.py', ...]' returned non-zero exit status 1

so every scheme ended with ANALYSIS_RC 1 even where the measurement and
pantheon_perf.json were perfectly good.

shutil.move() does copy+unlink when rename(2) says EXDEV.

NOTE: this patch touches ANALYSIS only, never measurement. For data already
collected against an earlier image, scripts/12_collect.sh applies the same
edit inside the throwaway analysis container at runtime, so the measurement
image id stays identical on both hosts (docs/decisions/002).

--- a/src/analysis/report.py
+++ b/src/analysis/report.py
@@
 import re
 import uuid
+import shutil
@@
-        os.rename(pdf_src_path, pdf_dst_path)
+        # ccbench-remote: tmp and data_dir are different filesystems
+        # (data_dir is a bind mount), so rename(2) gives EXDEV.
+        shutil.move(pdf_src_path, pdf_dst_path)
